the largest monument in europe is  located in leipzig germany and was built  on the location napoleon surrendered  [Music]  completed in 1913 the monument to the  battle of the nations is named after the  battle that took place a hundred years  earlier between napoleon and his allies  and the united armed forces of russia  prussia austria and sweden the fight  involved around 600 000 troops from over  20 countries and was the largest  european battle prior to world war one  at the base of the monument is the  archangel michael  above him are giant stone guards who  circle the structure  inside the ground floor there are eight  night statues who represent the fallen  soldiers they are joined by other  smaller figures known as the guardians  of the dead  these guardians watch over all the souls  who have been lost  all of these statues on the ground floor  are shadowed by the 31-foot giants on  the second story known as the hall of  fame  each of these represent the four  historic qualities attributed to the  german people  bravery  faith  sacrifice  and fertility  during the communist era when many  monuments were torn down this one  survived because the structure  commemorates a war when the russians and  germans fought together against a common  enemy  the scale of the monument inspires awe  with a height of nearly 300 feet  towering over leipzig and reminding all  who view it of the battles of the past  you
 

